    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. \n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule by adding a derived field, following this project's pattern for computed owner fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string enum (`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` (and its nested `MembershipTierEnum`) carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression computing the tier: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` (non-null) and email is present (non-null, non-empty), otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` pipeline already responds through `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so the tier is derived on read from the owner's stored fields. Full suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
